  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe four follow-up items of the second review of PR #2488 (#2517).\n\n1. **Two long files are split.**\n   - `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs`: upstream #2566 split this file into `commands/tool_import/mod.rs` and `commands/tool_import/report.rs` before this PR merged. The merge of `upstream/main` (d7982d620) keeps that layout and removes this branch's `tool_import_report.rs`. Thus this PR no longer changes the layout of `tool_import`.\n   - `crates/app/tests/tool_numbers.rs` (476 lines): the tests of numbers that never shift (#2442) and of legacy loads move to `tests/tool_numbers/stable.rs` (`#[path]` module, the pattern of `keep_law.rs`). Sizes now: 354 and 247 lines. The `#[test]` count of the binary goes from 10 to 13 (no test removed).\n2. **Two legacy-load tests** (in `stable.rs`):\n   - `a_legacy_project_numbers_by_name_order_not_by_document_order`: a pre-#2442 file whose entity order is not the name order. A save always writes name order, so the test moves `EM-0600-4FL` to the front of the entity list by hand (as an older build or an edit leaves a file). The load gives `EM-0400-2FL` T1 and `EM-0600-4FL` T2, and the post writes `T01` / `T02`.\n   - `a_legacy_project_mixing_numbered_and_unnumbered_tools_keeps_both`: `EM-0400-2FL` carries T7, `AA-SPARE` and `EM-0600-4FL` carry no number. The load keeps T7 and gives each other tool its place in the name-sorted list of all tools: `AA-SPARE` 1, `EM-0600-4FL` 3. The posted numbers then hold when a tool is added and when one is deleted.\n3. **No `u32::MAX` fallback.** The new `tool_numbers::assign` gives each unnumbered tool the lowest free number in order, and refuses by name when none of 1-99999 is free: `tool 'X' has no tool number and none of 1-99999 is free - give it its own tool number`. `tool_numbers::numbers` now returns `Result`:\n   - the post (`posting::op_streams_by`), `ImportTools` (`tool_import/mod.rs`) and the tool-table export (`tool_table::export`, from #2566) propagate the refusal;\n   - `clash` (the tool list page and the post's clash law) returns it as the refusal;\n   - `number_of` and `next_free` read it as `None` (the tool list export shows `?`; `next_free` is correct, because then no number is free).\n4. **No dead branch.** `SetToolNumber` keeps its number as a `u32` (`new` already refuses `None`, #2442) and has `number()`, as `AddTool` has. `crates/ui/src/state.rs` writes `tool <name> is now T<n>` from it, and the `None => \"number cleared\"` arm is gone.\n\nThe comment over the T/H law in `posting.rs` said \"else its 1-based position among the named tools in document order\". That is not true since #2442. It now says what the code does.\n\n## Tests\n\nReadings on the final head d7982d620 (after the merge of `upstream/main`):\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 261 steps, 0 failed.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`, #2568): 185 steps (`app heavy: lib`, `bins`, each heavy binary, `doc`; release, `--ignored`), 0 failed, 71 min.\n\nReadings before the merge (head 9d6151d35):\n\nPinned by (`camcraft-app`, `--test tool_numbers`):\n- `an_unnumbered_tool_with_no_free_number_is_refused_by_name` (`assign` with 99999 numbered tools and one without; then the lowest-free case).\n- `stable::a_legacy_project_numbers_by_name_order_not_by_document_order`.\n- `stable::a_legacy_project_mixing_numbered_and_unnumbered_tools_keeps_both`.\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_numbers`: 13 passed. With the name sort in `freeze_legacy_tool_numbers` removed, the name-order test fails (`first by name: left Some(2), right Some(1)`).\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, Linux, 12 cores, another build running on the box): 384 steps, 383 ok, 1 failed.\n- `app suites: tool_numbers`: 13 passed. `app suites: tool_import_modes`: 9 passed.\n- `ui suites: lib`: 1203 passed, 0 failed.\n- The other app and ui suites that the gate selected: ok.\n- `app suites: continuous_4axis_part`: FAIL, but not from this change. `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` on `upstream/main` (1ae4d061f) is project version 70, and `PROJECT_VERSION` is 71: `... is stale; regenerate with WRITE_GOLDEN=1: /version: 71 != 70`. This PR does not touch the project format or that example.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean in the files of this PR. One error is on `upstream/main` too: `clippy::drop_non_drop` at `crates/app/tests/import_step_thread.rs:133` (from d7bbf723a; #2794, fix in PR #2795). With `-A clippy::drop_non_drop` the run is clean.\n\nThe branch merges cleanly with `upstream/main` (`git merge-tree`).\n\nNo `.nc` or `.cl` golden file changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run in the app. The UI status text for a number change is the same as before (`tool <name> is now T<n>`, pinned by `setting_a_tool_number_is_a_command_with_undo`).\n- The refusal of item 3 is reached only by a fixture or a hand-made document with 99999 numbered tools. The test calls `assign` directly; it does not build 99999 tool entities.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Branch base: `upstream/main`. No context scout ran; this session did its own searches.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #2517\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
